<title>SWITZERLAND: Nestle joint venture sales rise.</title>
<headline>Nestle joint venture sales rise.</headline>
<dateline>VEVEY, Switzerland 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nestle SA said sales from its joint venture with General Mills Inc, called Cereal Partners Worldwide, rose by 23 percent to 689 million Swiss francs in the first 10 months of 1996.</p>
<p>Sales from the Galderma joint venture with French beauty products group L'Oreal were up 37 percent to 202 million francs.</p>
<p>Nestle said these were total sales of which it books 50 percent.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
